  "term": "repetitive strain injury",
  "definition": "Repetitive strain injury is a painful, harmful condition caused by overuse or overexertion of part of the musculoskeletal system, often in connection with work-related physical activity. It involves inflammation, pain, or reduced function in affected joints, bones, ligaments, or nerves.",
